# Raw HTTP request samples for idemresp (http://127.0.0.1:18080)

### 1. Create an order — first call executes exactly once

POST /v1/orders HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:18080
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: sample-order-0001

{"amount":1000,"currency":"USD","reference":"invoice-42"}

### 2. Retry unchanged — replays the stored response (no second side effect)

POST /v1/orders HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:18080
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: sample-order-0001

{"amount":1000,"currency":"USD","reference":"invoice-42"}

# Response header on the replay:
#   Idempotent-Replay: true

### 3. Same key with a different body — 409 conflict

POST /v1/orders HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:18080
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: sample-order-0001

{"amount":9999,"currency":"USD"}

# 409 {"error":"idempotency_key_conflict", ...}

### 4. Duplicate while the first request is still processing

POST /v1/orders HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:18080
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: sample-slow-0001

{"amount":1000,"currency":"USD"}

# 409 {"error":"request_in_progress", ...} with a Retry-After header.
# Re-issue the SAME request after completion to receive the stored response.

### 5. Read stored state

GET /v1/keys/sample-order-0001 HTTP/1.1
GET /v1/ledger?key=sample-order-0001 HTTP/1.1
GET /v1/orders?id=ord_xxxxxxxx HTTP/1.1

### 6. Fault injection headers (fake gateway only)

#   X-Fault: reset-before-charge   connection dropped, no charge
#   X-Fault: reset-after-charge    charged, then connection dropped (ambiguous)
#   X-Fault: hang                 charged, then no response (ambiguous)
#   X-Fault: error500             definite 500, no charge
#
#   X-Forward-Key: false          do not send Idempotency-Key to the gateway
#                                  (demonstrates the no-exactly-once boundary)
#   X-Pre-Commit-Delay: 1200ms    hold before the atomic commit
#   X-Post-Commit-Delay: 1200ms   hold after commit, before responding
#
# Crash injection additionally requires the server to run with -allow-crash:
#   X-Crash: before-commit | after-commit
